GearHead Arena: resume an initialized combat scene at its saved player input.

A live campaign save is written inside GetPlayerInput, after movement and the
confusion decision for that actor.  Record completed combat scene-entry setup
as an ordinary serialized scene numeric attribute.  Reset it only on a fresh
ScenePlayer deployment; restored live boards retain it.  On resume, rebuild
only derived shadows and displays, avoid repeating START/UPDATE/restocking,
and continue the interrupted actor pass before advancing the saved clock.
TacticsMain and TacticsTurn retain their existing behavior; this repair is
scoped to the ordinary CombatMain loop.  Legacy and startup saves without the
marker keep the original initialization path.  No save grammar or configuration
default changes are required.

Compact saves contain the complete string-attribute list, not design overrides.
Discard InitGear's default strings before loading, and store saved strings
verbatim, including empty values, just as WriteCGears writes them.

Upstream-Status: Not submitted [downstream native campaign resume fix]

